§ `Short names for the answers used below`

`C7 YES` MEANS `yes: all five elements of cl 7(1) are met; the invasion is actionable without proof of damage (cl 7(2))`
`C7 NOT SHOWN` MEANS `not shown: the Schedule's lists of intrusions and misuses are open, and none of the listed acts is said to have happened; whether what happened intruded upon your seclusion or misused information about you is for the court (cl 6(1), cl 7(1)(a), NOTHING-kind)`
`C7 NO EXPECTATION` MEANS `no: a person in your position would not have had a reasonable expectation of privacy in all the circumstances (cl 7(1)(b), the text's no)`
`C7 NOT INTENTIONAL` MEANS `no: the invasion was not intentional or reckless (cl 7(1)(c), the text's no)`
`C7 NOT SERIOUS` MEANS `no: the invasion was not serious (cl 7(1)(d), the text's no)`
`C7 PUBLIC INTEREST` MEANS `no: the public interest in your privacy did not outweigh the countervailing public interest (cl 7(1)(e), the text's no)`
`X 15(1)` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to a journalist, a journalist's employer or engager, or a person assisting a journalist, collecting, preparing for publication or publishing journalistic material (cl 15(1), the text's no)`
`X 15(1A)` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to publishing or distributing journalistic material that a journalist prepared for publication (cl 15(1A), the text's no)`
`X 16` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to an agency or State or Territory authority acting in good faith in its functions or powers (cl 16, the text's no)`
`X 16A` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to a staff member of an agency or State or Territory authority acting in good faith in its functions or powers (cl 16A, the text's no)`
`X 16B` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to a law enforcement body, or its staff acting in their duties, powers or functions (cl 16B(a), (b), the text's no)`
`X 17` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to an intelligence agency, or an ASIO affiliate or an agent or staff member of one acting in their functions or duties (cl 17(a), (aa), the text's no)`
`X INFO` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to an invasion involving a disclosure of information to, or information disclosed by, a law enforcement body or an intelligence agency (cl 16B(c), (d), cl 17(b), (c), the text's no)`
`X 18` MEANS `exempt: the Schedule does not apply to an invasion of privacy by a person under 18 (cl 18, the text's no)`
`X NONE` MEANS `no exemption in Part 3 of Schedule 2 applies on these facts`
`D 8(1)(a)` MEANS `defence: the invasion was required or authorised by or under an Australian law or a court or tribunal order (cl 8(1)(a))`
`D 8(1)(b)` MEANS `defence: you, or a person with lawful authority to do so for you, consented to it, expressly or impliedly (cl 8(1)(b))`
`D 8(1)(c)` MEANS `defence: the defendant reasonably believed it was necessary to prevent or lessen a serious threat to the life, health or safety of a person (cl 8(1)(c))`
`D 8(1)(d)` MEANS `defence: it was incidental to the exercise of a lawful right of defence of persons or property, and proportionate, necessary and reasonable (cl 8(1)(d))`
`D 8(2)` MEANS `defence: it was a publication, and the defendant would establish a defamation-law defence of absolute privilege, publication of public documents, or fair report of proceedings of public concern (cl 8(2), (3))`
`D NONE` MEANS `this clause gives no defence on these facts (cl 8, the text's no)`
`SUE YES` MEANS `yes: you have a cause of action in tort for a serious invasion of privacy, actionable without proof of damage (cl 7); you must start proceedings in time (cl 14)`
`SUE 20(1)(a)` MEANS `no: an action cannot be asserted, continued or enforced about an invasion of the privacy of a person who has died (cl 20(1)(a), the text's no)`
`SUE 20(1)(b)` MEANS `no: an action cannot be asserted, continued or enforced about an invasion of privacy by a person who has died (cl 20(1)(b), the text's no)`
`T IN` MEANS `in time: started before the day cl 14(1) of Schedule 2 sets`
`T ORDER` MEANS `out of time under cl 14(1), but in time under the court's order extending the time (cl 14(2), (3))`
`T NO ORDER` MEANS `out of time: not started before the day cl 14(1) sets, and there is no court order extending the time; the court may make one if satisfied it was not reasonable for you to start in time, for a day not later than 6 years after the invasion (cl 14, the text's no)`
`T LATE` MEANS `out of time: not started before the day cl 14(1) sets, nor before the day in the court's order (read as no later than 6 years after the invasion) (cl 14, the text's no)`
`R YES` MEANS `yes: you may complain to the Commissioner on behalf of all of them; you need not name them, count them or get their consent (ss 36(2), 38(2), (3))`
`R 36(2)` MEANS `no: one individual may complain for others only about an act or practice that may interfere with the privacy of 2 or more individuals, including that individual (s 36(2), the text's no)`
`R 38(1)` MEANS `no: a representative complaint may be lodged only if the class members have complaints against the same person or entity, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances, and raising a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 38(1), the text's no)`
`R WRITING` MEANS `not as it stands: a complaint must be in writing and must specify the respondent (s 36(3), (5))`
`R PARTICULARS` MEANS `not as it stands: a representative complaint must identify the class members and specify the nature of their complaints, the relief sought and the common questions of law or fact (s 38(2))`
`OWN NO` MEANS `no: a class member of a representative complaint is not entitled to lodge a complaint about the same subject matter (s 39, the text's no); you may withdraw first (s 38B(2))`
`OWN YES` MEANS `yes: s 39 does not stop you; an individual may complain to the Commissioner about an act or practice that may be an interference with their privacy (s 36(1))`
`ST NO DUTY` MEANS `no duty to give you a copy: the declaration does not require it (s 52A(1)(b), the text's no)`
`ST IN TIME` MEANS `given in time (s 52A(1)(b))`
`ST LATE` MEANS `given late: the copy was due within 14 days after the respondent received the determination, or the longer period allowed (s 52A(1)(b)); an organisation or small business operator must comply (s 55(d)), and you or the Commissioner may go to court to enforce the determination (s 55A)`
`ST ENDED` MEANS `not yet given, and the period has ended: the respondent has not complied (s 52A(1)(b)); you or the Commissioner may go to court to enforce the determination (ss 55A, 62)`
`CO YES` MEANS `yes: the court may order the entity to compensate you, including for injury to feelings or humiliation, or make another order to compensate or to prevent or reduce the loss; an amount ordered is a debt due to you (ss 25(1), (3), 25A(2), (5))`

§ `The dates module`

#ASSERT `1 Mar 2026` `plus calendar years` 1 EQUALS `1 Mar 2027`
-- 1 March 2026 is preceded by 28 February 2026 (2026 is a common year).
#ASSERT `the day before` `1 Mar 2026` EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
-- 2028 is a leap year.
#ASSERT `the day before` `1 Mar 2028` EQUALS `29 Feb 2028`
-- Fork F1: a 29 February birthday falls on 28 February in a common year.
#ASSERT `29 Feb 2008` `plus calendar years` 18 EQUALS `28 Feb 2026`
#ASSERT `the earlier of` `1 Sep 2026` `and` `1 Jul 2028` EQUALS `1 Sep 2026`
#ASSERT `the earlier of` `1 Oct 2028` `and` `1 Jul 2028` EQUALS `1 Jul 2028`
-- A day before the start counts as day 0.
#ASSERT `the day number of` `1 Jun 2025` `counted from` `1 Jul 2025` EQUALS 0

§ `Schedule 2 cl 7 -- the elements`

-- A hidden camera in a bathroom: recording private activities; all findings made.
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 YES`
-- Medical records disclosed to an employer.
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 YES`
-- Physical intrusion into the home.
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 YES`
-- Something else the court finds to be an intrusion or misuse.
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 YES`
-- None of the listed acts and no finding: the lists are open (NOTHING-kind).
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 NOT SHOWN`
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 NO EXPECTATION`
-- Negligent, not intentional or reckless.
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `C7 NOT INTENTIONAL`
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `C7 NOT SERIOUS`
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `C7 PUBLIC INTEREST`
-- Several elements fail: (b) is reported first, in the text's order.
#ASSERT `cl 7 -- do I have a cause of action` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `C7 NO EXPECTATION`
#ASSERT `cl 7(1)(a) -- did they invade my privacy` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `cl 7(1)(a) -- did they invade my privacy` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Schedule 2 Part 3 -- exemptions`

-- A neighbour with a camera.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
-- A professional journalist bound by a code, gathering news.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a journalist` TRUE TRUE `news, current affairs or a documentary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 15(1)`
-- Works as a journalist but bound by no standards or code: not a journalist (cl 15(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a journalist` TRUE FALSE `news, current affairs or a documentary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
-- Not working in a professional capacity (cl 15(2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a journalist` FALSE TRUE `news, current affairs or a documentary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
-- A journalist, but the material is not news, current affairs or a documentary (cl 15(3)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a journalist` TRUE TRUE `none of these` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
-- The publisher employing the journalist, publishing commentary on current affairs.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `the employer of a journalist, or a person engaging a journalist` TRUE TRUE `commentary or opinion on, or analysis of, news, current affairs or a documentary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 15(1)`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a person assisting a journalist in that person's professional capacity` TRUE TRUE `news, current affairs or a documentary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 15(1)`
-- A journalist doing something other than collecting, preparing or publishing journalistic material.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a journalist` TRUE TRUE `news, current affairs or a documentary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
-- Anyone sharing a news report a journalist prepared (cl 15(1A)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a person or business not listed below` TRUE TRUE `news, current affairs or a documentary` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 15(1A)`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a Commonwealth agency, or a State or Territory authority, that is not an intelligence agency or law enforcement body` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 16`
-- An agency not acting in good faith.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a Commonwealth agency, or a State or Territory authority, that is not an intelligence agency or law enforcement body` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a staff member of such an agency or authority` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 16A`
-- A police force: exempt whatever it was doing (cl 16B(a)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a law enforcement body` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 16B`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a staff member of a law enforcement body` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 16B`
-- A police officer acting outside their duties, powers or functions.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a staff member of a law enforcement body` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `an intelligence agency` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 17`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `an ASIO affiliate, or an agent or staff member of an intelligence agency` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X 17`
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `an ASIO affiliate, or an agent or staff member of an intelligence agency` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X NONE`
-- A business disclosing information to the police.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `X INFO`
-- Using information an intelligence agency disclosed.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `X INFO`
-- A 16-year-old schoolmate.
#ASSERT `Part 3 -- is the invasion exempt` `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `X 18`

§ `Schedule 2 cl 8 -- defences`

#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D NONE`
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D 8(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D 8(1)(b)`
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D 8(1)(c)`
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D 8(1)(d)`
-- Incidental to defence of property, but not proportionate, necessary and reasonable: (d)(ii) fails.
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `D NONE`
-- A fair report of court proceedings.
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `D 8(2)`
-- A publication without a related defence.
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `D NONE`
-- A related defence claimed, but not for a publication: (2)(a) fails.
#ASSERT `cl 8 -- does the defendant have a defence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `D NONE`

§ `Schedule 2 -- can I sue (the whole)`

-- A former partner secretly recorded intimate images; all findings made; no defence.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SUE YES`
-- The person whose privacy was invaded has died: the estate cannot sue.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` TRUE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SUE 20(1)(a)`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE TRUE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `SUE 20(1)(b)`
-- Under 18: the exemption comes before the elements.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Schedule does not apply` `X 18`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a journalist` TRUE TRUE `news, current affairs or a documentary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Schedule does not apply` `X 15(1)`
-- Not serious.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no cause of action` `C7 NOT SERIOUS`
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no cause of action` `C7 NOT SHOWN`
-- Consent.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you have a cause of action, but the defendant has a defence` `D 8(1)(b)`
-- Authorised by a warrant.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `you have a cause of action, but the defendant has a defence` `D 8(1)(a)`
-- No reasonable expectation, and consent too: the element is reported before the defence.
#ASSERT `Schedule 2 -- can I sue` FALSE FALSE `a person or business not listed below` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no cause of action` `C7 NO EXPECTATION`

§ `Schedule 2 cl 19 -- the single publication rule`

-- A repost by the same publisher of the same article: the first publication's day.
#ASSERT `cl 19 -- the day the invasion is taken to occur` `10 Jan 2026` TRUE TRUE `1 Jul 2025` EQUALS `1 Jul 2025`
-- Republished far more prominently: materially different.
#ASSERT `cl 19 -- the day the invasion is taken to occur` `10 Jan 2026` TRUE FALSE `1 Jul 2025` EQUALS `10 Jan 2026`
-- Published by someone unconnected with the first publisher.
#ASSERT `cl 19 -- the day the invasion is taken to occur` `10 Jan 2026` FALSE TRUE `1 Jul 2025` EQUALS `10 Jan 2026`

§ `Schedule 2 cl 14 -- time limits`

-- Adult; aware two months after: 1 year after awareness (1 Sep 2026) is earlier than 3 years after (1 Jul 2028); the day before.
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` EQUALS `31 Aug 2026`
-- Aware late: 3 years after the invasion (1 Jul 2028) is earlier than 1 year after awareness (1 Oct 2028).
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Oct 2027` EQUALS `30 Jun 2028`
-- An awareness day before the invasion counts as the day of the invasion.
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Jan 2025` EQUALS `30 Jun 2026`
-- Aged 15: before the 21st birthday (15 Mar 2031).
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `15 Mar 2010` `1 Aug 2025` `1 Aug 2025` EQUALS `14 Mar 2031`
-- On the 18th birthday: no longer under 18, so the adult rule.
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `1 Aug 2007` `1 Aug 2025` `1 Aug 2025` EQUALS `31 Jul 2026`
-- The day before the 18th birthday: under 18, so before the 21st birthday (1 Aug 2028).
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `1 Aug 2007` `31 Jul 2025` `31 Jul 2025` EQUALS `31 Jul 2028`
-- Born 29 Feb 2008, 18th birthday read as 28 Feb 2026 (fork F1): under 18 on 27 Feb 2026; 21st birthday 28 Feb 2029.
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `29 Feb 2008` `27 Feb 2026` `27 Feb 2026` EQUALS `27 Feb 2029`
-- On 28 Feb 2026 she is 18 (fork F1): adult rule, before 28 Feb 2027.
#ASSERT `cl 14(1) -- the last day to start proceedings` `29 Feb 2008` `28 Feb 2026` `28 Feb 2026` EQUALS `27 Feb 2027`
#ASSERT `cl 14(1)(a) -- was I under 18 when it happened` `1 Aug 2007` `31 Jul 2025` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `cl 14(1)(a) -- was I under 18 when it happened` `1 Aug 2007` `1 Aug 2025` EQUALS FALSE
-- The order's day may be at most 1 Jul 2031; proceedings must start before it.
#ASSERT `cl 14(4) -- the last day to start under the longest order` `1 Jul 2025` EQUALS `30 Jun 2031`
-- The last day.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `31 Aug 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `T IN`
-- One day late: 1 Sep 2026 is the day itself, not before it.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `1 Sep 2026` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `T NO ORDER`
-- Started on the day of the invasion.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `1 Jul 2025` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `T IN`
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `1 Mar 2027` TRUE `1 Jun 2027` EQUALS `T ORDER`
-- On the day in the order: not before it.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `1 Jun 2027` TRUE `1 Jun 2027` EQUALS `T LATE`
-- An order naming 1 Jan 2032, beyond 6 years, read as 1 Jul 2031 (fork F3); 30 Jun 2031 is before it.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `30 Jun 2031` TRUE `1 Jan 2032` EQUALS `T ORDER`
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `1 Jan 1990` `1 Jul 2025` `1 Sep 2025` `1 Jul 2031` TRUE `1 Jan 2032` EQUALS `T LATE`
-- Aged 15 at the time, starting the day before the 21st birthday.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `15 Mar 2010` `1 Aug 2025` `1 Aug 2025` `14 Mar 2031` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `T IN`
-- On the 21st birthday: too late.
#ASSERT `cl 14 -- are my proceedings in time` `15 Mar 2010` `1 Aug 2025` `1 Aug 2025` `15 Mar 2031` FALSE `1 Jan 2000` EQUALS `T NO ORDER`

§ `Schedule 2 cl 10 -- ending a claim early`

#ASSERT `cl 10 -- can my claim be ended early` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court may give judgment for the defendant, since it is satisfied you have no reasonable prospect of success (cl 10(1))`
#ASSERT `cl 10 -- can my claim be ended early` FALSE EQUALS `not under cl 10: the court is not satisfied you have no reasonable prospect of success (NOTHING-kind; the court's other powers remain, cl 10(2))`

§ `Schedule 2 cl 11 -- damages and the cap`

#ASSERT `cl 11 -- can I be awarded this kind of damages` `damages for economic loss` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award damages (cl 11(1)); damages for economic loss are outside the cap in cl 11(5)`
#ASSERT `cl 11 -- can I be awarded this kind of damages` `damages for non-economic loss` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award damages for non-economic loss (cl 11(1)), within the cap in cl 11(5)`
#ASSERT `cl 11 -- can I be awarded this kind of damages` `damages for emotional distress` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court may award damages for emotional distress (cl 11(3)), counted as non-economic loss within the cap in cl 11(5)`
-- Aggravated damages: never, even in exceptional circumstances.
#ASSERT `cl 11 -- can I be awarded this kind of damages` `aggravated damages` TRUE EQUALS `no: the court must not award aggravated damages (cl 11(2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `cl 11 -- can I be awarded this kind of damages` `exemplary or punitive damages` TRUE EQUALS `yes: in exceptional circumstances the court may award exemplary or punitive damages (cl 11(4)), within the cap in cl 11(5)`
#ASSERT `cl 11 -- can I be awarded this kind of damages` `exemplary or punitive damages` FALSE EQUALS `not in these circumstances: cl 11(4) gives exemplary or punitive damages in exceptional circumstances, and the court has not found them (NOTHING-kind)`
-- No defamation figure given: $478,550.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the cap` 0 EQUALS 478550
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the cap` 478550 EQUALS 478550
-- A higher defamation maximum governs.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the cap` 500000 EQUALS 500000
-- A lower defamation maximum: $478,550.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the cap` 400000 EQUALS 478550
-- Exactly at the cap.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the capped sum` 400000 78550 0 EQUALS 478550
-- One dollar over: cut to the cap.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the capped sum` 400000 78551 0 EQUALS 478550
-- Under the cap.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the capped sum` 300000 0 0 EQUALS 300000
-- Sum $550,000 against a $520,000 defamation maximum.
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the capped sum` 450000 100000 520000 EQUALS 520000
#ASSERT `cl 11(5) -- the capped sum` 450000 60000 520000 EQUALS 510000

§ `Schedule 2 cls 12 and 13 -- other remedies, apologies`

#ASSERT `cl 12 -- what else can the court order` TRUE EQUALS LIST `an account of profits (cl 12(2)(a))`, `an injunction, which may be granted at any stage of the proceedings (cl 12(2)(b), cl 9(1))`, `an order that the defendant apologise to you (cl 12(2)(c))`, `a correction order (cl 12(2)(d))`, `an order that the material obtained, made or misused in the invasion be destroyed, delivered up to you or dealt with as the court directs (cl 12(2)(e))`, `a declaration that the defendant has seriously invaded your privacy (cl 12(2)(f))`, `any other remedy the court thinks most appropriate, in addition to or instead of damages (cl 12(1))`
-- Nothing left to destroy or deliver up: (e) does not arise.
#ASSERT `cl 12 -- what else can the court order` FALSE EQUALS LIST `an account of profits (cl 12(2)(a))`, `an injunction, which may be granted at any stage of the proceedings (cl 12(2)(b), cl 9(1))`, `an order that the defendant apologise to you (cl 12(2)(c))`, `a correction order (cl 12(2)(d))`, `a declaration that the defendant has seriously invaded your privacy (cl 12(2)(f))`, `any other remedy the court thinks most appropriate, in addition to or instead of damages (cl 12(1))`
#ASSERT `cl 13 -- does their apology admit fault` TRUE EQUALS `no: an apology is not an admission of fault or liability and is not relevant to deciding fault or liability (cl 13, the text's no); the court may consider it in setting damages (cl 11(6)(a))`
#ASSERT `cl 13 -- does their apology admit fault` FALSE EQUALS `no apology has been made: cl 13 does not arise (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `Part V ss 36, 38 -- representative complaints`

-- A data breach affecting thousands of customers of one company.
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R YES`
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R 36(2)`
-- Complaints against different companies.
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R 38(1)`
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R 38(1)`
-- No substantial common issue.
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `R 38(1)`
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `R WRITING`
#ASSERT `ss 36, 38 -- can I lodge a representative complaint` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `R PARTICULARS`

§ `Part V ss 38B, 39 -- class members`

-- Lodged without consent: even after the inquiry began.
#ASSERT `s 38B(2) -- can I withdraw from the representative complaint` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes, at any time: it was lodged without your consent; give the Commissioner written notice (s 38B(2)(a)); you may then complain on your own (s 36, note to s 38B(2))`
#ASSERT `s 38B(2) -- can I withdraw from the representative complaint` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Commissioner has not begun to hold an inquiry into it; give the Commissioner written notice (s 38B(2)(b)); you may then complain on your own (s 36, note to s 38B(2))`
#ASSERT `s 38B(2) -- can I withdraw from the representative complaint` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: you consented to it, and the Commissioner has begun to hold an inquiry into it (s 38B(2)(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 39 -- can I lodge my own complaint` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `OWN NO`
-- A class member complaining about a different matter.
#ASSERT `s 39 -- can I lodge my own complaint` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `OWN YES`
-- Withdrawn from the representative complaint: no longer a class member.
#ASSERT `s 39 -- can I lodge my own complaint` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `OWN YES`

§ `Part V s 52 -- what a determination can give`

-- An individual complaint: reimbursement of expenses is available.
#ASSERT `s 52 -- what a determination can give me` FALSE EQUALS LIST `a declaration that the respondent interfered with privacy and must not repeat or continue the conduct (s 52(1)(b)(i))`, `a declaration that the respondent must take specified steps within a specified period so the conduct is not repeated (s 52(1)(b)(ia))`, `a declaration that the respondent must do any reasonable act or course of conduct to redress your loss or damage (s 52(1)(b)(ii))`, `a declaration that the respondent must prepare and publish or communicate a statement about the conduct (s 52(1)(b)(iia), s 52A)`, `a declaration that you are entitled to a specified amount of compensation, including for injury to feelings and humiliation (s 52(1)(b)(iii), (1AB))`, `a declaration that you are entitled to a specified amount to reimburse expenses reasonably incurred in making the complaint and in the investigation (s 52(3))`, `the determination is not binding or conclusive between the parties (s 52(1B)); it is enforced by proceedings in court (ss 55A, 62)`
-- A representative complaint: no reimbursement (s 52(3) other than, fork F8); s 52(4) payments.
#ASSERT `s 52 -- what a determination can give me` TRUE EQUALS LIST `a declaration that the respondent interfered with privacy and must not repeat or continue the conduct (s 52(1)(b)(i))`, `a declaration that the respondent must take specified steps within a specified period so the conduct is not repeated (s 52(1)(b)(ia))`, `a declaration that the respondent must do any reasonable act or course of conduct to redress your loss or damage (s 52(1)(b)(ii))`, `a declaration that the respondent must prepare and publish or communicate a statement about the conduct (s 52(1)(b)(iia), s 52A)`, `a declaration that you are entitled to a specified amount of compensation, including for injury to feelings and humiliation (s 52(1)(b)(iii), (1AB))`, `on a representative complaint, compensation of specified amounts or amounts worked out in a specified manner, with provision for paying the class members (s 52(4))`, `the determination is not binding or conclusive between the parties (s 52(1B)); it is enforced by proceedings in court (ss 55A, 62)`

§ `Part V s 52A -- the statement`

#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` FALSE `1 Mar 2026` 14 FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ST NO DUTY`
-- Received 1 Mar 2026; 14 days after is 15 Mar 2026, the last day.
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 14 TRUE `15 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ST IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 14 TRUE `16 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ST LATE`
-- A longer period of 30 days allowed: 31 Mar 2026 is the last day.
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 30 TRUE `31 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ST IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 30 TRUE `1 Apr 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ST LATE`
-- A period under 14 days is read as 14.
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 7 TRUE `15 Mar 2026` `1 Jun 2026` EQUALS `ST IN TIME`
-- Not yet given on the last day itself.
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 14 FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `15 Mar 2026` EQUALS `not yet given, and the period has not ended` `15 Mar 2026`
#ASSERT `s 52A -- has the respondent given me the statement in time` TRUE `1 Mar 2026` 14 FALSE `1 Jan 2000` `16 Mar 2026` EQUALS `ST ENDED`

§ `Part V ss 55A, 62 -- enforcing a determination`

-- Against a company.
#ASSERT `ss 55A, 62 -- can I enforce the determination` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you (or any class member) may start proceedings in the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) to enforce it; the court decides afresh whether there was an interference with privacy (s 55A(1)(a), (5), (8))`
#ASSERT `ss 55A, 62 -- can I enforce the determination` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not you: the determination followed an investigation on the Commissioner's own initiative (s 52(1A)); ss 55A(1) and 62(3) name the complainant only for a determination on a complaint (NOTHING-kind); the Commissioner may enforce it`
#ASSERT `ss 55A, 62 -- can I enforce the determination` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the agency has not complied; you (or any class member) may apply to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2) for an order directing it to comply (s 62(1)-(3), (6))`
#ASSERT `ss 55A, 62 -- can I enforce the determination` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: no application may be made until the time for seeking Administrative Review Tribunal review has expired, or the Tribunal's decision on review has come into operation (s 62(5), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 55A, 62 -- can I enforce the determination` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 62 gives no application while the agency is complying with the determination (s 62(1), (2), the text's no)`

§ `Part IIIA ss 25, 25A -- compensation orders`

#ASSERT `ss 25, 25A -- the last day to apply` `10 Jun 2020` EQUALS `10 Jun 2026`
-- Fork F1 and F9.
#ASSERT `ss 25, 25A -- the last day to apply` `29 Feb 2024` EQUALS `28 Feb 2030`
-- On the sixth anniversary: in time (fork F9).
#ASSERT `ss 25, 25A -- can I get a compensation order` TRUE TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `10 Jun 2026` EQUALS `CO YES`
#ASSERT `ss 25, 25A -- can I get a compensation order` TRUE TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `11 Jun 2026` EQUALS `no: the application must be made within 6 years of the day the cause of action accrued (ss 25(2)(b), 25A(4)(b), the text's no)`
-- No penalty order or conviction yet.
#ASSERT `ss 25, 25A -- can I get a compensation order` FALSE TRUE `10 Jun 2020` `1 Jan 2021` EQUALS `no: the court may make these orders only after a civil penalty order against the entity, or a finding of guilt of an offence, under Part IIIA (ss 25(1)(a), 25A(1)(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `ss 25, 25A -- can I get a compensation order` TRUE FALSE `10 Jun 2020` `1 Jan 2021` EQUALS `no: the loss or damage must have resulted from the contravention or the offence (ss 25(1)(b), 25A(1)(b), the text's no)`
